      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{table}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0047",
      "sha256": "c81cc6cbd414d183e75305acf6368839770497aab27b704731945d2ffd5e7a97",
      "char_start": 33500,
      "char_end": 34109,
      "n_chars": 609,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0048",
      "sha256": "db224e17c6f971d818241dcb4b3cf8073e164b62e6479bb0c7909bc302e57657",
      "char_start": 34111,
      "char_end": 35226,
      "n_chars": 1115,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Across ten seeds the $k$-means solutions are stable. The seed standard deviation of their ARI is 0.000 for raw"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0049",
      "sha256": "d18cdc47338a83638d16a4994b688e989f974089e0be7adcf8b3b9ec4b887924",
      "char_start": 35228,
      "char_end": 36035,
      "n_chars": 807,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The two foundation models do not behave as one category. ECGFounder clusters strongly while HuBERT-ECG does no"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0050",
      "sha256": "ef6f5eb701fcd5b77c748c7598a8adc3cb8a57d402b192a360e8f10fe524facf",
      "char_start": 36037,
      "char_end": 36084,
      "n_chars": 47,
      "section": "Clustering by representation and algorithm",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{Separability is not clusterability}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0051",
      "sha256": "1625afa2cc548b3475685e384f0f4da21c571c633a8c9601399200a21d6d00d1",
      "char_start": 36086,
      "char_end": 37256,
      "n_chars": 1170,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The supervised ceilings (last column of Table~\\ref{tab:main}, Fig.~\\ref{fig:sep}) expose the gap between separ"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0052",
      "sha256": "78fc3a080c3fa27d5ca528bba5be7e65386f89f10bd474c0e98fd38555367d81",
      "char_start": 37258,
      "char_end": 37880,
      "n_chars": 622,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Each result has a likely explanation, and the study did not test these mechanisms directly. ECGFounder was pre"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0053",
      "sha256": "5085990acaabcf6e7b60e66e0f6230635319c3a5b505a3400b4bfd122fbc97a8",
      "char_start": 37882,
      "char_end": 38629,
      "n_chars": 747,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "HuBERT-ECG was pretrained by self-supervision without diagnostic labels \\cite{hubertecg2024}, and here it saw "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0054",
      "sha256": "b8a84288b9d8ef1e4608523b57e696bdc01b7d5a6889d70051b52609ed427f23",
      "char_start": 38631,
      "char_end": 39161,
      "n_chars": 530,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Raw flattening and the conv-AE score at chance for different reasons. With $k$-means, raw flattening places on"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0055",
      "sha256": "864edea17b169a5d12ed6cc0d8f1679c90c8daaeca23892f0e932dccd67b6cf6",
      "char_start": 39163,
      "char_end": 39966,
      "n_chars": 803,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\begin{figure}[t]"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0056",
      "sha256": "b3eb476ff58189ffd6535514e14b0a4144a30aa0d3d2711f3e346b848b326a4d",
      "char_start": 39968,
      "char_end": 40000,
      "n_chars": 32,
      "section": "Separability is not clusterability",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\subsection{The silhouette trap}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0057",
      "sha256": "b539a29832e878beb7c1cbd7dd50b9a22b04363793ca1638f4af087ab1aac298",
      "char_start": 40002,
      "char_end": 40639,
      "n_chars": 637,
      "section": "The silhouette trap",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Internal indices mislead here in a specific, reproducible way. Raw flattening with Ward attains a silhouette o"
    },
    {
