      "block_id": "B0070",
      "sha256": "d082247dd47fe0ea20c97ecd8ed518d3d1a7079e38a37096ba96c1baefba4df1",
      "char_start": 46406,
      "char_end": 47598,
      "n_chars": 1192,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The practical reading holds for the settings tested: two binary tasks, five clusterers, two named foundation m"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0071",
      "sha256": "b87d5f563331e8c2e6bb8a7c909d07836a0a7d497fa219984f60dd3d30643b9a",
      "char_start": 47600,
      "char_end": 47959,
      "n_chars": 359,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "The result also reframes the original master's project. Its conclusion that the bottleneck is the representati"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0072",
      "sha256": "a11df5b589a52107b88ac36fe49a13db802f36984cd16e9311d0df1b222b6911",
      "char_start": 47961,
      "char_end": 49511,
      "n_chars": 1550,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "We propose no new algorithm. The separability-versus-clusterability effect is known \\cite{sslclustering2025}, "
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0073",
      "sha256": "afaa0b7efcda8f9ead6b600c7b846ef2de31476b8cf28f0710776b2932380b7a",
      "char_start": 49513,
      "char_end": 49557,
      "n_chars": 44,
      "section": "Discussion",
      "first_line_excerpt": "\\section{Limitations}\\label{sec:limitations}"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0074",
      "sha256": "1cd464ed81b4a89dbfbe110e226873debf7c90dcbf64beea5e0f0f88980c15cc",
      "char_start": 49559,
      "char_end": 50647,
      "n_chars": 1088,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "ECGFounder expects 500\\,Hz input. Because bulk streaming of the 500\\,Hz records was rate-limited at the source"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "B0075",
      "sha256": "9e7c83cb704400b8016f1e8f6e41c597a77d8b621866091d568b5d3cd78d1883",
      "char_start": 50649,
      "char_end": 51275,
      "n_chars": 626,
      "section": "Limitations",
      "first_line_excerpt": "Both tasks are binary, and the study makes no claim about multi-class rhythm structure. Public 12-lead databas"
    },
    {
